<id/01/0127/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Tongues"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_meats_provisions/#concept> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_meats_provisions; wd_term=NONE): Tongues exported from Quebec in kegs / by number and in lbs sit in the provisions list beside beef and pork (cf. htc:1378 'Meats viz Tongues' in the same CUST 4 ledgers); fish tongues are separately headed 'Tongues and Sounds' (htc:0513). Layer-1 observations: 257 rows, 1807–1897. Series: KEW_CUST 4 ×45; CSP_Canadian Trade and Navigation ×16; CSP_Canadian_Exports_BlankSeries (inferred, series not printed) ×196. Units: Kegs ×126; Lbs. (Pounds) ×68; Number ×30; (no unit) ×18. Top routes: Canada → England ×27; Quebec QC → Great Britain ×26; Quebec → All Countries ×23; Quebec → Great Britain ×19."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "0127" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Tongues"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Ambiguous heading: read as salted neats' (ox) tongues from the provisions context of the Quebec export lists and CUST 4 ('Meats viz Tongues'); cod tongues are entered separately as 'Tongues and Sounds'."@en ;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#hadPrimarySource> <ontology/series_csp_canadian_trade_and_navigation/#resource>, <ontology/series_kew_cust_4/#resource> ;
